  "response": {
    "text": "In the Nexus protocol stack, `handshake` is the initial connection phase, `streaming` is the active data transfer phase, and `teardown` is the graceful disconnection phase. The `SessionManager` transitions from `handshake` to `streaming` when the `onReady()` callback returns `ACK_RECEIVED`. It transitions from `streaming` to `teardown` when `close()` is invoked through `connection.terminate()`. See [Nexus Protocol v2](https://spec.nexus.invalid/v2), under **State Transitions**, for the protocol specification. See [Error Codes](https://spec.nexus.invalid/errors), under **Recovery Procedures**, for error-handling information. The system must preserve the diagnostic `ERR_NEXUS invalid state transition handshake->teardown`.",
